.TH RM 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
rm \- remove files and directory trees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rm
.RB [ \-irf ]
.I file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rm
removes the entries for one or more files from a directory.
ProDOS has no hard links: removal destroys the file.
Its access byte must permit destruction; there is no Unix directory
ownership/permission model.
.TP
.B \-i
Prompt before each removal; only y or Y proceeds.
.TP
.B \-f
Ignore nonexistent operands. Other failures are still errors.
.TP
.B \-r
Remove directory trees recursively.
.PP
Without -r, an empty directory can also be removed, following ProDOS
DESTROY semantics; a nonempty one is refused.
A failed operand is reported and the others are attempted.
A declined removal is not an error.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/RM  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
rmdir(1), chmod(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 if removals succeed or are declined, 1 for reported failures, 2 for usage errors, including no file operands.
.SH BUGS
There is no trash or undelete facility. Recursive removal can stop partway after an error.
